<site xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">69176167</site>	<item>
		<title>Southwest’s New Platinum Status Adds Too Little—10 Ways Rapid Rewards Should Fix Its New Program</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/southwests-new-platinum-status-adds-too-little-10-ways-rapid-rewards-should-fix-its-new-program/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/southwests-new-platinum-status-adds-too-little-10-ways-rapid-rewards-should-fix-its-new-program/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 19:34:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Airlines]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[elite status]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[southwest airlines]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259225</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Southwest Airlines is adding Platinum status to Rapid Rewards, but someone who already has A-List Preferred and Companion Pass won't get much new. A third checked bag, earlier boarding, and a higher advertised earning bonus (offset by lower base-earning on higher fares) are very modest additions considering they're launching a new top tier.  Gold, the replacement for A-List Preferred, already gets the same seats.]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://viewfromthewing.com/southwests-new-platinum-status-adds-too-little-10-ways-rapid-rewards-should-fix-its-new-program/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			<enclosure url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/southwest-infinite-legroom-exit-row.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg" />
	<media:content url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/southwest-infinite-legroom-exit-row.jpg" fileSize="0" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="959" width="1278" />
<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">259225</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>American Airlines Says AAdvantage Is Its Edge—These 10 Changes Would Make That True</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/american-airlines-says-aadvantage-is-its-edge-these-10-changes-would-make-that-true/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/american-airlines-says-aadvantage-is-its-edge-these-10-changes-would-make-that-true/#comments</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 16:58:36 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Airlines]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[american aadvantage]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[american airlines]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259220</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Here are ten changes that would make earning American miles and status more worthwhile. Most have precedents at other airlines. Some are things American has already done, and could simply bring back. ]]></description>
		
