		<item>
		<title>China Eastern’s Ex-Chairman Gets 14 Years For $10 Million In Bribes—He Didn&#8217;t Follow Xi Jinping&#8217;s Instructions</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/china-easterns-ex-chairman-gets-14-years-for-10-million-in-bribes-he-didnt-follow-xi-jinpings-instructions/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/china-easterns-ex-chairman-gets-14-years-for-10-million-in-bribes-he-didnt-follow-xi-jinpings-instructions/#comments</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 16:12:58 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Airlines]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[china eastern]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259285</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[China Eastern's former chairman has been sentenced to 14 years in prison in a bribery case involving more than $10 million. The court says Liu Shaoyong sold favors over a period stretching from 2002 through 2023, using positions at both China Eastern and China Southern. He'd left China Eastern in 2022 with a glowing sendoff from the board. Nearly three years later, the Communist Party announced it was investigating him.]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://viewfromthewing.com/china-easterns-ex-chairman-gets-14-years-for-10-million-in-bribes-he-didnt-follow-xi-jinpings-instructions/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>4</slash:comments>
		
		
			<enclosure url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/former-china-eastern-ceo-sentenced.jpg" length="502061" type="image/jpeg" />
	<media:content url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/former-china-eastern-ceo-sentenced.jpg" fileSize="502061" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1008" width="1792" />
<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">259285</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Air Serbia Flight Turns Back As Spy Onboard Accused Of Bypassing Security</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/air-serbia-flight-turns-back-as-spy-onboard-accused-of-bypassing-security/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/air-serbia-flight-turns-back-as-spy-onboard-accused-of-bypassing-security/#comments</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:56:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Airlines]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259286</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[An Air Serbia flight to Moscow made it as far as Lithuania before turning around and flying back to Belgrade, where everyone had to get off and go through security again. Local reporting says Serbia's former intelligence chief was allowed to board without completing his screening. He says he was being targeted by political opponents.]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://viewfromthewing.com/air-serbia-flight-turns-back-as-spy-onboard-accused-of-bypassing-security/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>1</slash:comments>
		
		
			<enclosure url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/air-serbia.jpg" length="514888" type="image/jpeg" />
	<media:content url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/air-serbia.jpg" fileSize="514888" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1008" width="1792" />
<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">259286</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Hotel CEOs Reveal Where They Think Travel Is Headed—But AI Could Make Them Lower Room Prices</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/hotel-ceos-reveal-where-they-think-travel-is-headed-but-ai-could-make-them-lower-room-prices/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/hotel-ceos-reveal-where-they-think-travel-is-headed-but-ai-could-make-them-lower-room-prices/#comments</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:04:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Hotels]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259224</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[GHA Discovery asked hotel CEOs what will shape their business over the next few years, and 87% expect AI assistants to be among the most important booking channels by 2030. They expect hotel websites and loyalty programs to matter more than online travel agencies.
]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://viewfromthewing.com/hotel-ceos-reveal-where-they-think-travel-is-headed-but-ai-could-make-them-lower-room-prices/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
