<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">259222</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>British Airways Flight Attendant Hands Passenger Paper Towels And A Spray Bottle For Urine-Soaked Seat On 8-Hour Flight</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/british-airways-flight-attendant-hands-passenger-paper-towels-and-a-spray-bottle-for-urine-soaked-seat-on-8-hour-flight/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/british-airways-flight-attendant-hands-passenger-paper-towels-and-a-spray-bottle-for-urine-soaked-seat-on-8-hour-flight/#comments</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 19:34:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Airlines]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[british airways]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259227</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[A British Airways passenger says she boarded an eight hour flight from Miami to London Heathrow, sat down, and discovered her seat was soaked in urine. Her pants were wet, and she says a flight attendant told her there were no empty seats and she could have paper towels and a tiny bottle of antibacterial cleaning spray to deal with the mess - she couldn't even have an extra blanket.]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://viewfromthewing.com/british-airways-flight-attendant-hands-passenger-paper-towels-and-a-spray-bottle-for-urine-soaked-seat-on-8-hour-flight/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>10</slash:comments>
		
		
			<enclosure url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2qGdh.jpg" length="668407" type="image/jpeg" />
	<media:content url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2qGdh.jpg" fileSize="668407" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="1008" width="1792" />
<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">259227</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>JetBlue Raises Bag Fees Again—One Checked Bag Can Cost $140 Roundtrip, Other Airlines Likely To Follow</title>
		<link>https://viewfromthewing.com/jetblue-raises-bag-fees-again-one-checked-bag-can-cost-140-roundtrip-other-airlines-likely-to-follow/</link>
					<comments>https://viewfromthewing.com/jetblue-raises-bag-fees-again-one-checked-bag-can-cost-140-roundtrip-other-airlines-likely-to-follow/#comments</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gary Leff]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 18:07:03 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Airlines]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[checked bag fees]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[jetblue]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://viewfromthewing.com/?p=259238</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[JetBlue has raised checked bag fees again. Your first bag now costs at least $50 each way on domestic flights, and as much as $70 if you pay within 24 hours of departure on a peak travel date. That's $140 roundtrip for one bag.]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://viewfromthewing.com/jetblue-raises-bag-fees-again-one-checked-bag-can-cost-140-roundtrip-other-airlines-likely-to-follow/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>12</slash:comments>
		
		
			<enclosure url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/phoenix-baggage-claim.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg" />
	<media:content url="https://viewfromthewing.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/phoenix-baggage-claim.jpg" fileSize="0" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" height="864" width="1920" />
<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">259238</post-id>	</item>
